Quiz02_04:
30 points plus up to 20 bonus points
(isAVL and genAVLBST)
Please state the status of this question:
1. Incomplete 
2. Solved with testing?
3. Solved without testing?
If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.

I chose to solve this one with testing. For isAVL, I used a recursive helper that returns the height of a subtree if it is AVL, or -1 if it is not AVL. This checks each node only once, so the AVL test runs in linear time. For genAVLBST, I used the AVL maximal height idea which is to make the tree as tall as possible, each node should have one subtree of height h - 1 and the other of height h - 2. This gives the recurrence N(h) = 1 + N(h - 1) + N(h - 2). I tested isAVL on an empty tree and tested genAVLBST by printing the maximal height for 1 million nodes.

